{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact local SH-1 head b7f70899dcdaf3afb9e4cbc37c6963278a6e13c9, tree 6ab30963229b65dbc1e45ce558aaf55146ef9ffa, all four artifacts, for request 54ad1427 under implementation promise 1283e597 and my promise 54109b9c. I read the head from the shared object store. SH-1 does what request 15c42203 asks for Grow, and it adds no Counter or Lending row.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Rows. `APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS` in `apps/room/wrangler.grow.jsonc` and the `GROW` entry of `SCREEN_HOSTS` in `apps/sandbox/wrangler.rollout.jsonc` now hold one equal descriptor. Its screen origin is https://grow.inguz.space, its room origin is https://dap-grow.inguz.workers.dev, its directory is sc_cu5bjlh3…, its item is 2, and its presentation is sha256:2a3adecf…. The presentation equals `examples/grow/release-identifiers.json` at this head, and the directory, item and presentation equal the installed Grow 2.0.0 screen address that the request reads as 404. The old descriptor named the retired room sc_ryghgist… and presentation 5bd818a7. The comment above the room row now says what the row serves.\n- Test. The new case in `scripts/deploy-smoke.test.mjs` reads every `apps/room/wrangler*.jsonc` file with `parseConfig`. For each descriptor, the case requires exactly one sandbox service whose `service` is that Worker's name and whose entrypoint is `ApplicationScreenService`. It then requires the sandbox `SCREEN_HOSTS` list to equal the expected list, so a row on either side alone fails. That is item 3 of the request.\n- Control. `controls/2026-11-14-sh1-development-control-attempt1` beside the gate log fails the new case with \"room and sandbox screen descriptors must match, with no row on one side alone\" when only the room side's presentation changes. This is the direct assertion for the rule.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-sh1-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 a5af9374…, as END 499274ba states. Its first lines name head 3753c02c and tree d971e732 with 0 changed files. It reports Node 196, one more than main for the new case, and Counting 55, `scope-scale: omitted-by-gate`, and ends \"gate passed\". The stage log shows the new case passing. From 3753c02c to the head only the implementation note changes.\n- Scope. Main 863ca6b2 is an ancestor, and origin main is still 863ca6b2. The four artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --name-only 863ca6b2 b7f70899`. The commit-message check passes: 3 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each row still lives in two files, but the test now holds them equal, so the second copy can no longer drift unseen. Request 15c42203 asks for the cost of one new screen host for the cost review, and promise 1283e597 states it. A single source for both files is a later decision.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The descriptor maps one screen origin to one installed presentation of one room, through the existing route and service binding. It changes no trust row, packet, register, archive policy or publisher key. The sandbox still maps only grow.inguz.space.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The head reuses the existing descriptors, `parseConfig` and the deploy smoke owner.\n\nThe gate and the control prove the configuration, not the deployed screen. After the landing, the planner deploys `dap-grow` and the sandbox and reads the screen address. None of the four paths matches `page-browser.yml` or `views-browser.yml`, so SH-1 owes no browser workflow by itself. This approval authorizes no push, landing, deployment or install. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:092d107ef142f5d6a0ac874e4d6437883c24ef86","binding":"assigned","head":"b7f70899dcdaf3afb9e4cbc37c6963278a6e13c9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:54109b9ce484396467e48aef2808c8d7914817d9\"]